# T62 — build-context allowlist for backend-rs/.
#
# WHY: the Dockerfile's build context is backend-rs/ (see compose.yaml `rust`
# service). Without this file the context shipped `target/` — the shared cargo
# target dir is tens of GB (orchestration log records a 6.4 GB cache; the
# current shared target is ~44 GB) — so every `docker build` first had to TAR
# and upload gigabytes the image never reads. Excluding it is the single
# biggest CI/local build-speed win in this task.
#
# The COPY lines that MATTER (Dockerfile) are:
#   Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, .sqlx/, migrations/, openapi.json, src/, public/
#
# SCOPE DISCIPLINE: this file excludes only what is LARGE or SENSITIVE.
# `tests/` is DELIBERATELY NOT excluded even though `cargo build --release`
# never compiles it — Cargo.toml declares `[[test]] name = "api" path =
# "tests/api.rs"`, and cargo resolves an EXPLICIT target's path at manifest
# load, so a context without tests/ can fail the build. The bytes it saves
# are not worth the risk; target/ is the actual problem.

# --- never an image input, and large or inert -------------------------------
target/
docker-compose.test.yml

# --- secrets / env (never bake; Settings validates at boot) ----------------
# The Dockerfile contract gate greps for DATABASE_URL; nothing here reaches
# the image because COPY lists files explicitly, but keep them out of the
# context tarball too (defence in depth).
.env
.env.*

# --- editor/OS noise --------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# --- KEEP (do not exclude) --------------------------------------------------
# .sqlx/      committed offline query cache — the build needs NO database.
# migrations/ compile-time inputs (sqlx::migrate! embed).
# openapi.json include_str! embed (served + printed).
# public/     frontend dist copied in by CI BEFORE `docker build`
#             (the SPA fallback contract; not in git).
# src/        the crate.
# tests/      see SCOPE DISCIPLINE above — kept for the explicit [[test]] path.
#
# Note: `!` re-includes are unnecessary because none of the exclusion patterns
# above can match these names. If a future pattern is added (e.g. `*.json`),
# re-check that openapi.json and public/ survive it.
